{"authored" [{"question" "q-73752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-6y=10 \\\\ -x+3y=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "49fa51f522404fd460abdd2efa66d61eb076760af464dbcf1bc91ce7c1769d9b" "basis" 1654 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & 10 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=5 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-3y=5.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=5+3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5+3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "49fa51f522404fd460abdd2efa66d61eb076760af464dbcf1bc91ce7c1769d9b" "basis" 1654 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a5075986389a705f9a1167392eeca9fd79bef4e22632515d2329da419fc6c2ca" "basis" 1654 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "49fa51f522404fd460abdd2efa66d61eb076760af464dbcf1bc91ce7c1769d9b" "basis" 1654 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3+5y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "49fa51f522404fd460abdd2efa66d61eb076760af464dbcf1bc91ce7c1769d9b" "basis" 1654 "verification" "/home/jake/Deve