t "No solution"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/state.json" "file_sha256" "49fa51f522404fd460abdd2efa66d61eb076760af464dbcf1bc91ce7c1769d9b" "basis" 1654 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044402/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-42153" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=2 \\\\ 3x+9y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082306/state.json" "file_sha256" "b10c8b75e5269cb253a1dedd2ffd28a1a27e7fa7fdf19eb2e35fae46f8f2afdd"} {"question" "q-42153" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=2 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx+3y=2.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=2-3y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2-3y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082306/state.json" "file_sha256" "b10c8b75e5269cb253a1dedd2ffd28a1a27e7fa7fdf19eb2e35fae46f8f2afdd"} {"question" "q-42153" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082306/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4ca33098478668c2d711c0c7803b3baff9193da942527bc4ffd30169d9a99f47"} {"question" "q-42153" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082306/state.json" "file_sha256" "b10c8b75e5269cb253a1dedd2ffd28a1a27e7fa7fdf19eb2e35fae46f8f2afdd"} {"question" "q-42153" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082306/state.json" "file_sha256" "b10c8b75e5269cb253a1dedd2ffd28a1a27e7fa7fdf19eb2e35fae46f8f2afdd"} {"question" "q-42153" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2-3y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082306/state.json" "file_sha256" "b10c8b75e5269cb253a1dedd2ffd28a1a27e7fa7fdf19eb2e35fae46f8f2afdd"} {"question" "q-42155" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082306/state.json" "file_sha256" "b10c8b75e5269cb253a1dedd2ffd28a1a27e7fa7fdf19eb2e35fae46f8f2afdd"} {"question" "q-42155" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=3 \\\\ 0x+0y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any pair of numbers $x,y$ is a solution of the final equation $0x+0y=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of a single equation\n\n$$\nx-y=3.\n$$\n\nThe first variable $(x)$ is the basic variable, and the second variable $(y)$ is the free variable. Solving for the basic variable $(x)$ in terms of the free variable $(y),$ we get $x=3+y,$ and the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3+y \\\\ y=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ is an arbitrary number. \n\nIn vector form, the general solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082306/state.json" "file_sha256" "b10c8b75e5269cb253a1dedd2ffd28a1a27e7fa7fdf19eb2e35fae46f8f2afdd"} {"question" "q-42155" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082306/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4ca33098478668c2d711c0c7803b3baff9193da942527bc4ffd30169d9a99f47"} {"question" "q-42155" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082306/state.json" "file_sha256" "b10c8b75e5269cb253a1dedd2ffd28a1a27e7fa7fdf19eb2e35fae46f8f2afdd"} {"question" "q-42155" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3-y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082306/state.json" "file_sha256" "b10c8b75e5269cb253a1dedd2ffd28a1a27e7fa7fdf19eb2e35fae46f8f2afdd"} {"question" "q-42155" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3+y \\\\ y\\end{aligned}],\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082306/state.json" "file_sha256" "b10c8b75e5269cb253a1dedd2ffd28a1a27e7fa7fdf19eb2e35fae46f8f2afdd"} {"question" "q-73751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-10y=-5 \\\\ 2x-4y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082306/state.json" "file_sha256" "b10c8b75e5269cb253a1dedd2ffd28a1a27e7fa7fdf19eb2e35fae46f8f2afdd"} {"question" "q-73751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we set up the augmented matrix for the system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=-1 \\\\ 0x+0y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0x+0y=4$ has no solution. It simplifies to $0=4,$ which is a false statement.\n\nSo, there is no pair $x,y$ that satisfies both equations in the system. Consequently, the overall system has no solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14082306/state.json" "file_sha256" "b10c8b75e5269cb253a1dedd2ffd28a1a27e7fa7fdf19eb2e35fae46f